<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29752" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mōrus</span></b> , a, um,
		adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μωρός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>foolish, silly</i>
			(Plautin.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amor mores hominum moros et morosos facit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 3, 2, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut hoc utimur more moro molestoque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Men. 4, 2, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mōrus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>a fool,
			simpleton</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morus es,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 3, 1, 78</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mōra</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>a foolish
			woman</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 2, 4, 17</span></i>.—
				Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mōrē</span></b> , <i>foolishly</i> (Plautin.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">more hoc fit atque stulte,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Stich. 5, 1, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
